  {
    "id": "CO2-1",
    "statement": "A feature that strictly CONTAINS an edit grows by the inserted bases and still describes its own feature. POST /sequences/{id}/edit inserting 30 bases at position 3000 of NC_001699.1 must store all 28 features; the five whose interval strictly contains position 3000 (source, prim_transcript, gene, CDS, exon) must each have the containing part's end moved by +30 with its start unmoved, and must extract exactly the pre-edit bases of that feature with the 30 inserted bases spliced in at the corresponding offset \u2014 30 bases longer, not byte-identical. Byte-identity is the wrong standard for a containing feature: those inserted bases are now its bases, which is what shift_annotations does and therefore what CO-14 asks for.",
